---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import cambridgeCover from '../assets/images/books/cambridge-companion.jpg';
import postmodernismCover from '../assets/images/books/postmodernism-and-beyond.png';
import fatherAndSonCover from '../assets/images/books/father-and-son.png';

const cambridgeUrl =
	'https://www.amazon.com/Cambridge-Companion-Martin-Companions-Literature/dp/1009618040/';
const postmodernismUrl = 'https://link.springer.com/book/10.1057/9780230598478';
const fatherAndSonUrl = 'https://uwpress.wisc.edu/books/2549.htm';
---

<Layout
	title="Books"
	description="Gavin Keulks — three books, 2003–2026, on Kingsley and Martin Amis and the postwar English and Irish novel."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Books</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">
				On Kingsley and Martin&nbsp;Amis and the postwar English&nbsp;novel.
			</p>
		</header>

		<article class="book">
			<a class="book-cover" href={cambridgeUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				<Image
					src={cambridgeCover}
					alt="Cover of The Cambridge Companion to Martin Amis"
					widths={[176, 208, 352, 416]}
					sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 11rem, 13rem"
				/>
			</a>
			<div class="book-body">
				<h2>
					<a href={cambridgeUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Cambridge&nbsp;Companion to Martin&nbsp;Amis</a>
				</h2>
				<p class="book-meta">Cambridge University Press, 2026</p>

				<p>
					International in scope, this collection features the work of fourteen
					scholars from five different countries, ranging from established
					experts to new scholars of Amis&rsquo;s work.
				</p>
				<p>
					Available in print and digital from{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.cambridge.org/us/universitypress/subjects/literature/english-literature-after-1945/cambridge-companion-martin-amis?format=PB&isbn=9781009618045" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Cambridge University Press</a
					>, Amazon (<a
						href="https://www.amazon.com/Cambridge-Companion-Martin-Companions-Literature/dp/1009618040" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>US</a
					>,{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.amazon.co.uk/Cambridge-Companion-Martin-Companions-Literature/dp/1009618040/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>UK</a
					>), Waterstones (<a
						href="https://www.waterstones.com/book/the-cambridge-companion-to-martin-amis/gavin-keulks/9781009618076" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>hardback</a
					>,{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.waterstones.com/book/the-cambridge-companion-to-martin-amis/gavin-keulks/9781009618045" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>paperback</a
					>), and other booksellers. Read the{' '}
					<a
						href="https://assets.cambridge.org/97810096/18045/excerpt/9781009618045_excerpt.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>introduction</a
					>{' '}and{' '}
					<a
						href="https://assets.cambridge.org/97810096/18076/frontmatter/9781009618076_frontmatter.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>front matter</a
					>, including the list of contributors and a chronology.
				</p>
				<p>
					The book was spotlighted at a full-day book launch and podcast event
					in London on 25 August 2026, with panels featuring seven of my fourteen
					contributors on editing Amis, Amis&rsquo;s longevity, and the future of
					Amis studies. See the{' '}
					<a href="https://martinamisweb.com/after-amis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>After Amis</a
					>{' '}landing page on The Martin&nbsp;Amis Web for teaser videos, full
					program, and other materials.
				</p>

				<p class="book-links">
					Google Books:{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Cambridge_Companion_to_Martin_Amis/0Bnq0QEACAAJ?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Preview</a
					>
				</p>
				<p class="book-links">
					Reviews:{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.irishtimes.com/culture/books/review/2026/08/31/cambridge-companion-to-martin-amis-book-underscores-unresolved-difficulty-of-placement-in-the-literary-canon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Irish Times</a
					> | New Statesman
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="book">
			<a class="book-cover" href={postmodernismUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				<Image
					src={postmodernismCover}
					alt="Cover of Martin Amis: Postmodernism and Beyond"
					widths={[176, 208, 352, 416]}
					sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 11rem, 13rem"
				/>
			</a>
			<div class="book-body">
				<h2>
					<a href={postmodernismUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Martin Amis: Postmodernism and Beyond</a>
				</h2>
				<p class="book-meta">Palgrave Macmillan, 2006</p>

				<p>
					The first book of original essays published on Amis, this edited
					collection features the work of twelve scholars from six different
					countries.
				</p>
				<blockquote class="review">
					<p>
						&ldquo;This collection represents a real advance in Martin Amis
						studies. Twelve informed and exciting essays by an international range
						of leading Amis scholars and critics explore his novels and literary
						journalism from a wide variety of aspects and provide a rich source
						of fresh insights and perspectives. In a theoretically sophisticated
						but accessible way, they examine the structure, language and
						significance of his work and its controversial engagements with
						postmodernity, class, gender and Holocaust. The collection also
						contains an invaluable bibliography of Amis&rsquo;s prolific
						nonfiction. This book is essential reading for all those interested in
						Amis and contemporary writing.&rdquo;
					</p>
					<cite>Nicolas Tredell, editor of <em>The Fiction of Martin Amis</em></cite>
				</blockquote>
				<p class="book-links">
					Google Books:{' '}
					<a
						href="https://books.google.com/books/about/Martin_Amis_Postmodernism_and_Beyond.html?id=4Cd_DAAAQBAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Preview</a
					>
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="book">
			<a class="book-cover" href={fatherAndSonUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				<Image
					src={fatherAndSonCover}
					alt="Cover of Father and Son: Kingsley Amis, Martin Amis and the British Novel Since 1950"
					widths={[176, 208, 352, 416]}
					sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 11rem, 13rem"
				/>
			</a>
			<div class="book-body">
				<h2><a href={fatherAndSonUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Father and Son</a></h2>
				<p class="book-subtitle">
					Kingsley Amis, Martin Amis, and the British Novel Since 1950
				</p>
				<p class="book-meta">University of Wisconsin Press, 2003</p>

				<blockquote class="review">
					<p>
						&ldquo;<em>Father and Son</em> will be important to specialists in the
						field as well as to students of the twentieth-century novel
						generally. It provides the only extended treatment of a unique
						literary genealogy.&rdquo;
					</p>
					<cite>James Diedrick, author of <em>Understanding Martin Amis</em></cite>
				</blockquote>
				<blockquote class="review">
					<p>
						&ldquo;Keulks&rsquo; book is holding and absorbing, filled with
						excellently shrewd and steady analysis of selected novels, essays and
						interviews set in the context of the status and future of the
						realistic novel, the transition from modernism to postmodernism, and
						the existential condition of post-World War II life.&rdquo;
					</p>
					<cite>
						Dale Salwak, author of <em>Kingsley Amis: Modern Novelist</em> and{' '}
						<em>Kingsley Amis: In Life and Letters</em>
					</cite>
				</blockquote>
				<p class="book-links">
					Google Books:{' '}
					<a
						href="https://www.google.com/books/edition/Father_and_Son/9Aip8etZ_hwC?hl=en&gbpv=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Preview</a
					>
				</p>
				<p class="book-links">
					Review: Robert S. Baker,{' '}
					<em>Contemporary&nbsp;Literature</em> 46.3 (Fall&nbsp;2005): 544&ndash;54
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.page-intro {
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 0.6vw, 1.3rem);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.book {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 13rem 1fr;
		gap: 2.75rem;
		padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.book:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.book-cover {
		display: block;
		align-self: start;
	}

	.book-cover :global(img) {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
	}

	.book-body h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1rem + 1.3vw, 1.7rem);
		line-height: 1.15;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.book-body h2 a {
		color: var(--color-ink);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.book-body h2 a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
		text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
	}

	.book-subtitle {
		margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		line-height: 1.35;
	}

	.book-meta {
		margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.book-body p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.review {
		margin: 1.35rem 0;
		padding: 0 0 0 1.3rem;
		border: 0;
		border-left: 2px solid var(--color-line-strong);
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-style: normal;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.review p {
		margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
	}

	.review cite {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.book-body .book-links {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.book-body .book-links:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.book-links a {
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.book {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}

		.book-cover {
			max-width: 11rem;
		}
	}
</style>
